{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head d48f1e4ee9b42676e1ee817be75e3e288e6b9f02. This head touches no card path, as I checked against the workflow's list, so no citation is owed. **No person and no deployed Worker has run this, and it does not meet J5's acceptance.** The scene runs on the deployed Worker after the planner deploys.\n\n**The shared words: the card and `needs_you` behave as before.** I read the move line by line. `questionRows` is the same two loops that left `repo-in-ai.ts`, and `questionOffers` is the same three conditions that left `decision.ts`, with the same asker check and the same filter on `bodyAt`. The card's words now come from `whyLine`, `reasonLines`, `READING_LEAVES_OPEN` and `APPROVAL_LIMIT`, with the same text. `j5.test.mjs`, `s4.test.mjs` and `needs-you.scope.test.ts` pass, so the golden bytes hold.\n\n**`data.ts`: right.** `questionsOf` works from one summary. `factOf` refuses a name that disagrees with the record: a wrong scope, a wrong sequence or a wrong hash gives no answer, and it does not offer a press on a guess. The answer's `bodyAt` is that checked fact, so a press binds the text that this read names. If the question is edited before the press, `stale-question` refuses it. `approve` takes `on: \"\"`, which `send` reads as no item, and that fits an act that opens an `approval`. Its `bodyAt`, `request` and `verdict` match the act's fields, and `decide` names its question, as the two 200 answers show.\n\n**`main.ts`: right.** Each answer goes through `send`, so `lockedByCopy` and the read before the keep from c44e1ad7 both apply. Its button is disabled while a send is pending or uncertain, and it appears only when `actsOn` offers that act. I looked at `1-opened.png`. The screen reads as the scene asks, and the raw forms stay under **Advanced**.\n\n**The relative import: I accept it for now.** A package for one file of words costs a lockfile change, and the kernel-boundary check reports 0 refusals. The risk is a later import that drags room reads or Node into the Page, and a comment is the only guard against it. The bundle's build and `assets.test.ts` would catch a Node import. A larger import would show only as a bigger module. If a second file of `apps/views` wants to cross this line, make it a package then.\n\n**The limits.**\n- **The done-when says \"no value typed by a script\".** The script typed the device link, which a person pastes. That is the right reading, since no value of the answer itself is typed, and your note states it.\n- **A request with no reason.** **Request changes** signs with no comment, though the act has a `comment` field. It is the same on the card, and the scope accepts it. A person who chooses it gives the asker no reason, and the planner may want a text box at this screen's next edit.\n- **A Brief that the Page cannot compare.** The card withholds its answers when its retained Brief differs. The Page shows the digest and offers the answers. Approval binds the text and not the Brief, and the sentence on screen says so, so I accept this.\n- **The cost.** Each open question costs one entry read and one text read when the issue opens, and `ask` allows 64. So a very busy lane could cost about 128 sequential reads per view. That is fine for today's rooms. A transport error in one of those reads rejects the whole issue view, as `textOf`'s other callers can.\n- **Raw digests.** The Brief and Rule lines show raw digests, as the card does.\n\n**The sentence that I asked for** in 853a7367 is corrected in the two-process note, and the new script is on the second table of `docs/testing.md`.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is 76cfdec4…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 9541f0ba, exit 0, with 3538 and 1024 tests. After the gate, the head adds only the note and its manifest. I ran `page-questions.scope.test.ts` and `needs-you.scope.test.ts` (3 passed), `view.test.ts`, `sending.test.ts` and `assets.test.ts` (19 passed), `j5.test.mjs` and `s4.test.mjs` (22 pass), `security-entry-points` (10 pass), check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (1002, 0 broken), check-commit-messages (2, 0 flagged) and check-kernel-boundary. The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the browser script or the controls, and I read the one screenshot named above.\n\n**Architecture.** One set of words now serves both surfaces, which is what the request asks. The Page's own data stays in `data.ts`.\n\n**Security.** These rows grant nothing, as the page says. Each press goes through the existing send path, and the scope judges it. Author text reaches the page as text through `h`, and a question's title goes through `shownText`. A viewer's offers come from `room.me.actions`, which the scope does not trust.\n\n**Simplification.** This removes a duplicate of the offer rule and of the row rule. Nothing more to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ecd0d8684c57afdb6579b6ff9a27e70326b69219","binding":"assigned","head":"d48f1e4ee9b42676e1ee817be75e3e288e6b9f02","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45c9eb9c42c9d7ff57a6cff99b0e9afed4cca577\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b6a8333ed538d6f8cc832141eb39278e0731c294\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45c9eb9c42c9d7ff57a6cff99b0e9afed4cca577","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}